ulty Retirement Options Row 2 Perks and Privileges Retiree Health Coverage Retirement Planning Row 3 Supplemental Retirement Planning Tenured Faculty Retirement Transition Program Virginia Retirement System (VRS) Menu Home Careers Job Openings About Mason Accessibility Employee Type Definitions Employment Posters Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Military Members and Veterans Perks and Incentives Dual Career (Spouse/Partner) Support Title IX New Employees Onboarding Portal Campus Map Faculty and Staff Engagement Faculty Retirement Options Military Members and Veterans New Instructional Faculty Support Relocation Resources Supplemental Retirement Planning Well-Being Current Employees Benefits Employee Assistance Programs Employee and Workforce Relations Flexible Work Leave Life/Work Support Resources Performance Engagement Supervisory and Leadership Development Retirement Planning Payroll Resources Reward and Recognition Professional Development Tuition Resources Well-Being HR Network Classification and Compensation All-Inclusive Diversity, Access, and Engagement Recruitment Toolkit EPAF/Non-Benefited Onboarding eWork / PeopleAdmin / Search Resources (OLD) Exit Process Hiring Procedures Toolkit HR News HR Liaison Reference Guide International Employment Personnel Action Policies and Handbooks Position Creation and Maintenance Supervisors All-inclusive Diversity, Access and Engagement Faculty and Staff Engagement Hiring Procedures Toolkit Onboarding Toolkit for Supervisors Performance Engagement Policies and Handbooks Supervisory and Leadership Development Reward and Recognition Talent Acquisition Payroll Resources Retirement Retirement Announcements Faculty Incentive Retirement Plan Faculty Retirement Options Retiree Perks and Privileges Retiree Health Coverage Retirement Planning Supplemental Retirement Planning Tenured Faculty Retirement Transition Program Virginia Retirement System Forms HR News Directories HR Directory HR Liaison Directory Quick Links Connect with Us Discounts | Patriot Perks eWork / PeopleAdmin / Search Resources (OLD) Holiday Schedule HR Data Requests Income and Employment Verification Life Changes MasonLEAPS MyMasonHR Patriot Web Policies and Handbooks Contact Us Mason's Onboarding Portal Employee Type Definitions Mason’s Onboarding Portal Employee Type Definitions Onboarding Instructional, Research, and Adjunct Faculty Onboarding Administrative and Professional Faculty Onboarding Classified Staff Onboarding Wage and Student Wage Onboarding Toolkit for Supervisors New Employee FAQ Select a section below to learn more. Instructional and Research Faculty Expand Instructional faculty appointments focus primarily on teaching undergraduate and graduate courses. These positions may have the following designations: tenure (without term), tenure-track, term (non tenure-track). Research and clinical faculty assignments focus primarily on research or clinical practice. Instructional and research faculty may hold the following ranks: Instructor (Research Associate), Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Adjunct Faculty Expand Adjunct faculty are part-time appointments appointed to fulfill the teaching and advising responsibilities associated with a specific course (or a set of specified courses) on a semester by semester basis. Administrative and Professional Faculty Expand Administrative Faculty and Professional Faculty are normally referred to collectively as Administrative/Professional Faculty (A/P faculty). Both require advanced learning acquired by prolonged formal instruction and/or specialized training and work experience. Administrative faculty positions are generally senior administrators who perform work related to the management of the educational and general activities of the university. Professional faculty positions may support education, research, University Life, and other such activities and may typically hold positions as librarians, counselors, coaches, physicians, or lawyers. Classified Staff Expand Classified staff hold positions that include a wide range of roles within the University. They are typically non-teaching employees and may be classified as either exempt (not overtime eligible) or non-exempt (overtime eligible). These employees are covered by the provisions of the Virginia Personnel Act (Title 2.2, § 2.2-2900 of the Code of Virginia), once they have completed the 12-month probationary period. Wage Employment Expand Non-student wage employees’ primary relationship with Mason is intended to cover peak workloads, seasonal or short-term needs. These types of positions are all part-time and typically pay is based on an hourly basis. Student Employment Expand Student employment is designed to provide financial support while attending Mason. Student wage employees’ primary relationship with Mason is the pursuit of an academic degree. Student employees are students first and foremost and, in recognition of this, should be limited to a total of 20 hours per week. During semester breaks students may work up to an average of 29 hours per week. Types of student employment may be categorized in work study positions, student wage (hourly) positions, or graduate assistantships. Find Us! Office Number: 4100 Alan and Sally Merten Hall GPS Address: 4441 George Mason Boulevard, Fairfax, Va. 22030 Mailing Address: 4400 University Drive, Mailstop 3C3 Contact Us! Email: hr@gmu.edu Phone: 703-993-2600 Fax: 703-993-2601 Connect With Us! Airplane icon that links to subscribe to HR & Payroll subscription page Subscribe to our newsletter Facebook Icon that Links to Mason's HR's Facebook Page /GeorgeMasonHR Twitter Icon that Links to Mason's HR's Twitter Page @GeorgeMasonHR Instagram Icon that Links to Mason's HR's Instagram Page @GeorgeMasonHR LinkedIn Icon that Links to Mason's HR LinkedIn Page /GeorgeMasonHR (opens in new tab) Mission Statement | Accessibility | Disclaimers Copyright © 2026 George Mason University Scroll To Top"
    },
